{"parentUuid":"6cffccd3-99ba-4613-9e41-36bbd876ff8c","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"9bdfc07b-8ff1-4e95-9c88-de7440fd6192","agentId":"a247aee484158d5cb","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Vv5iih4TA67CkhE4hV5mYG","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t=== engine-architect [orchestrator/process/Game Engine Chief Architect] parent=None ws=governance profiles=['all'] targets=[] plats=None\n2\t  purpose: Owns the engine's overall architecture: requirements and configuration profiles, layering and module boundaries, the contract registry, global conventions, build/integrate/buy decisions and cross-domain arbitration. Final authority on the boundaries between skills.\n3\t  nonresp: Running the ADR, fitness-function and anti-legacy process -> architecture-governance || Scheduling work across agents and the ownership ledger -> program-orchestration || Architecture inside a domain (e.g. shading-path choice) -> render-architect\n4\t  provides: ['C-ARCH']  consumes: []  tool: []  impl: []\n5\t=== architecture-governance [orchestrator/process/Architecture Governance] parent=engine-architect ws=governance profiles=['all'] targets=[] plats=None\n6\t  purpose: Runs architecture as an evidence-backed, governed process: ADR lifecycle with revisit conditions, technology radar with maturity tiers and promotion criteria, automated fitness functions (layering, dependency direction, contract conformance), anti-legacy review, coding standard.\n7\t  nonresp: Making the architecture decisions themselves -> engine-architect || Grading sources and running spikes -> research-evidence || Test definition of done -> test-architect\n8\t  provides: ['C-ADR']  consumes: []  tool: []  impl: []\n9\t=== program-orchestration [orchestrator/process/Engine Program Orchestration] parent=engine-architect ws=governance profiles=['all'] targets=[] plats=None\n10\t  purpose: Turns architecture into coordinated multi-agent work: decomposes milestones into tasks by skill territory, keeps the ownership ledger and territory locks, sequences integration through vertical slices, routes contract change requests, and schedules critic gates.\n11\t  nonresp: Deciding architecture -> engine-architect || CI mechanics -> ci-cd-automation || Release versioning -> build-release-architect\n12\t  provides: ['C-ORCH']  consumes: ['C-PROD']  tool: []  impl: []\n13\t=== research-evidence [cross-cutting/process/Research & Evidence] parent=engine-architect ws=governance profiles=['all'] targets=[] plats=None\n14\t  purpose: Research discipline for every major decision: finds and grades authoritative evidence (production talks, platform docs, peer-reviewed work, reproducible benchmarks), classifies techniques as established / emerging / experimental / speculative, and runs spikes where literature is thin.\n15\t  nonresp: Making the decision (the owning skill does, via an ADR) -> architecture-governance || Benchmark infrastructure -> perf-benchmarking\n16\t  provides: ['C-EVID']  consumes: []  tool: []  impl: []\n17\t=== performance-architect [cross-cutting/process/Performance Architect] parent=engine-architect ws=performance profiles=['all'] targets=[] plats=None\n18\t  purpose: Owns performance as a discipline: the hypothesis → instrumentation → measurement → optimization → regression-test loop, budgets per subsystem and hardware tier, the scalability / device-profile framework, and performance gates.\n19\t  nonresp: Optimizing subsystem code (via C-PERF findings) -> owning-skill || Instrumentation API -> observability-telemetry || Benchmark harness -> perf-benchmarking || Runtime scalability machinery -> runtime-scalability\n20\t  provides: ['C-BUDGET', 'C-PERF']  consumes: []  tool: []  impl: []\n21\t=== perf-benchmarking [expert/process/Benchmarking & Performance Regression] parent=performance-architect ws=performance profiles=['all'] targets=[] plats=None\n22\t  purpose: Benchmark harnesses (micro and representative-workload scenes), automated capture, statistical analysis (variance, significance), regression detection and bisection, dashboards.\n23\t  nonresp: Setting budgets -> performance-architect || CI infrastructure -> ci-cd-automation\n24\t  provides: ['C-BENCH']  consumes: ['C-INSTR', 'C-BUDGET']  tool: []  impl: []\n25\t=== cpu-performance [expert/process/CPU Performance Engineering] parent=performance-architect ws=performance profiles=['all'] targets=[] plats=None\n26\t  purpose: CPU microarchitecture-level optimization and review: cache and memory-access patterns, vectorization audits, contention and false sharing, hybrid-core and power-aware tuning, PGO/LTO.\n27\t  nonresp: Owning subsystem code -> owning-skill || Math library -> math-simd-numerics || Scheduler design -> job-system-task-graph || Changing subsystem code (findings route via C-PERF) -> owning-skill\n28\t  provides: []  consumes: ['C-INSTR', 'C-BUDGET', 'C-TASK']  tool: []  impl: []\n29\t=== gpu-performance [expert/process/GPU Performance Engineering] parent=performance-architect ws=performance profiles=['all'] targets=[] plats=None\n30\t  purpose: GPU performance analysis and review: occupancy, bandwidth, cache behavior, barrier and async-compute overlap, vendor tools across PC, console and mobile, GPU power.\n31\t  nonresp: Render graph scheduling design -> render-graph-scheduling || Shader authoring for features -> render-architect\n32\t  provides: []  consumes: ['C-INSTR', 'C-BUDGET', 'C-RG', 'C-RHI']  tool: []  impl: []\n33\t=== loading-streaming-performance [expert/process/Loading & Hitch Performance] parent=performance-architect ws=performance profiles=['all'] targets=[] plats=None\n34\t  purpose: End-to-end load time, startup time and hitch elimination (PSO compilation, streaming stalls, GC pauses, synchronous waits), IO throughput analysis.\n35\t  nonresp: IO backend implementation -> async-io-storage || PSO cache implementation -> rhi-core || Streaming policy -> resource-streaming-architect\n36\t  provides: []  consumes: ['C-INSTR', 'C-BUDGET', 'C-IO', 'C-RES']  tool: []  impl: []\n37\t=== test-architect [cross-cutting/process/Test Architect] parent=engine-architect ws=quality profiles=['all'] targets=[] plats=None\n38\t  purpose: Test strategy and architecture: per-subsystem test pyramid, frameworks, the test definition of done every skill must meet, contract tests, test content, coverage and mutation policy, flakiness policy.\n39\t  nonresp: Running pipelines -> ci-cd-automation || Performance regression -> perf-benchmarking || Rendering image validation -> render-validation\n40\t  provides: ['C-TEST']  consumes: []  tool: []  impl: []\n41\t=== render-validation [expert/process/Rendering Validation] parent=test-architect ws=quality profiles=['all'] targets=[] plats=None\n42\t  purpose: Rendering correctness validation: golden-image tests with perceptual metrics, tolerances per GPU/driver, comparisons against the reference path tracer, graphics API validation in CI.\n43\t  nonresp: Fixing rendering features -> render-architect || Material furnace tests (defines them; this skill runs them) -> material-system\n44\t  provides: []  consumes: ['C-RG', 'C-RHI', 'C-RSCENE', 'C-RT?']  tool: []  impl: []\n45\t=== functional-automation-soak [expert/process/Functional Automation & Soak] parent=test-architect ws=quality profiles=['all'] targets=[] plats=None\n46\t  purpose: Game-level automation: scripted and bot playthroughs, smoke/boot tests, soak and stability runs (memory growth, leaks), hardware/OS compatibility matrix, network harnesses and server load tests.\n47\t  nonresp: Unit test frameworks -> test-architect || Device-farm infrastructure -> ci-cd-automation\n48\t  provides: []  consumes: ['C-GAME?', 'C-INPUT?', 'C-NET?']  tool: []  impl: []\n49\t=== robustness-fuzzing [expert/process/Robustness & Fuzzing] parent=test-architect ws=quality profiles=['all'] targets=[] plats=None\n50\t  purpose: Robustness engineering: fuzzing every untrusted-input parser (assets, packets, saves, scripts, mods), sanitizer build policy, fault injection (IO errors, OOM, device lost), concurrency stress and schedule perturbation.\n51\t  nonresp: Threat model -> security-engineering || Fixing parsers -> serialization-schema\n52\t  provides: []  consumes: ['C-SER', 'C-IO']  tool: []  impl: []\n53\t=== certification-compliance [expert/process/Certification & Compliance] parent=test-architect ws=quality profiles=['all'] targets=[] plats=None\n54\t  purpose: Tracks and pre-validates external requirements: platform certification (TRC/XR/Lotcheck class), age ratings, privacy law, accessibility law (CVAA, EAA), third-party licenses and SBOM, photosensitivity testing.\n55\t  nonresp: Implementing platform features -> platform-architect || Implementing accessibility features -> accessibility\n56\t  provides: ['C-CERT']  consumes: ['C-A11Y?', 'C-SVC']  tool: []  impl: []\n57\t=== security-engineering [cross-cutting/process/Security Engineering] parent=engine-architect ws=quality profiles=['all'] targets=[] plats=None\n58\t  purpose: Threat modeling and trust boundaries for every untrusted input, secure-coding and memory-safety policy, supply-chain security, secrets, anti-tamper boundary, privacy engineering, mod/UGC sandbox policy.\n59\t  nonresp: Cheat detection -> anti-cheat-integrity || Fuzzing campaigns -> robustness-fuzzing || Transport encryption implementation -> network-transport\n60\t  provides: ['C-TRUST']  consumes: []  tool: []  impl: []\n61\t=== anti-cheat-integrity [expert/runtime/Anti-Cheat & Game Integrity] parent=security-engineering ws=online profiles=['all'] targets=['client', 'headless-client', 'server', 'tools'] plats=None\n62\t  purpose: Cheat resistance for online games: server-authoritative validation patterns (movement, hits, economy), rate limiting, anomaly signals, integration boundary for client anti-cheat middleware.\n63\t  nonresp: Replication design -> replication || Transport encryption -> network-transport\n64\t  provides: []  consumes: ['C-NET?', 'C-PREDICT?', 'C-PHYS?', 'C-GAME?', 'C-SVC?', 'C-LIVE?']  tool: []  impl: []\n65\t=== observability-telemetry [cross-cutting/runtime/Observability & Telemetry] parent=engine-architect ws=foundation profiles=['all'] targets=['client', 'headless-client', 'server', 'tools'] plats=None\n66\t  purpose: Instrumentation substrate: structured logging, trace zones (CPU, GPU, IO, memory), counters and metrics, profiler integrations, in-game stats, development and live telemetry with privacy consent; zero cost when compiled out.\n67\t  nonresp: Crash capture -> crash-diagnostics || Debug drawing and consoles -> visual-debugging-tools || Perf budgets -> performance-architect\n68\t  provides: ['C-INSTR']  consumes: ['C-PAL', 'C-BASE', 'C-SYNC']  tool: []  impl: []\n69\t=== crash-diagnostics [cross-cutting/runtime/Crash & Hang Diagnostics] parent=engine-architect ws=foundation profiles=['all'] targets=['client', 'headless-client', 'server', 'tools'] plats=None\n70\t  purpose: Crash, hang and GPU-fault capture and reporting: minidumps, symbolication, bucketing and triage, GPU crash dumps, watchdogs, OOM reports, assert reporting.\n71\t  nonresp: Emitting GPU breadcrumbs -> rhi-core || Symbol server infrastructure -> ci-cd-automation\n72\t  provides: ['C-CRASH']  consumes: ['C-PAL', 'C-BASE', 'C-INSTR']  tool: []  impl: []\n73\t=== determinism-replay [cross-cutting/runtime/Determinism & Replay] parent=engine-architect ws=foundation profiles=['all'] targets=['client', 'headless-client', 'server', 'tools'] plats=None\n74\t  purpose: Defines determinism levels (none, same-binary, cross-platform) per subsystem and the floating-point and parallel-execution rules that achieve them; owns input/state record-replay and desync detection.\n75\t  nonresp: Rollback netcode -> prediction-rollback || Deterministic math implementation -> math-simd-numerics\n76\t  provides: ['C-DET', 'C-SNAPSHOT', 'C-REPLAY']  consumes: ['C-MATH', 'C-TASK', 'C-SER@C-SNAPSHOT', 'C-FRAME@C-SNAPSHOT']  tool: []  impl: []\n77\t=== hot-reload-iteration [cross-cutting/runtime/Hot Reload & Iteration] parent=engine-architect ws=foundation profiles=['all'] targets=['client', 'headless-client', 'server', 'tools'] plats=None\n78\t  purpose: Owns the reload protocol (change detection, dependency invalidation, state preservation) that assets, shaders, scripts, config and C++ live coding plug into; measures edit → see latency.\n79\t  nonresp: Each system's own reload implementation (via C-RELOAD) -> owning-skill || Build system -> build-system-toolchains\n80\t  provides: ['C-RELOAD']  consumes: ['C-RES', 'C-MOD', 'C-REFL']  tool: ['C-BUILD']  impl: []\n81\t=== accessibility [cross-cutting/runtime/Accessibility] parent=engine-architect ws=ui profiles=['all'] targets=['client', 'tools'] plats=None\n82\t  purpose: Maps XAG/GAG and legal requirements to engine features and owns subtitles and captions, screen-reader/TTS/STT hooks, colorblind and contrast modes, text scaling, motion and photosensitivity options, assist hooks, and their validation.\n83\t  nonresp: Input remapping implementation -> input-system || UI layout engine & subtitle presentation -> ui-architect || Colorblind passes -> post-color-hdr || Legal compliance sign-off -> certification-compliance\n84\t  provides: ['C-A11Y', 'C-A11YRT']  consumes: ['C-TEXT', 'C-PAL', 'C-DIALOGUE?']  tool: []  impl: []\n85\t=== api-lifecycle-migration [cross-cutting/process/API Lifecycle & Engine Migration] parent=engine-architect ws=governance profiles=['all'] targets=[] plats=None\n86\t  purpose: Public API surface, semantic versioning and deprecation, ABI policy, engine-upgrade tooling (codemods, data upgraders) and LTS policy, so projects can move across engine versions.\n87\t  nonresp: Data schema mechanisms -> serialization-schema || Plugin loading -> plugin-system\n88\t  provides: ['C-API']  consumes: ['C-SER', 'C-REFL', 'C-RELEASE']  tool: []  impl: []\n89\t=== plugin-system [expert/runtime/Plugin System] parent=api-lifecycle-migration ws=foundation profiles=['all'] targets=['client', 'headless-client', 'server', 'tools'] plats=None\n90\t  purpose: Plugin architecture: manifests, discovery, dependency resolution, load phases, binary vs source plugins, isolation, distribution format.\n91\t  nonresp: Mods & UGC -> modding-ugc || Module linking internals -> core-runtime-architect\n92\t  provides: ['C-PLUGIN']  consumes: ['C-MOD', 'C-BASE', 'C-API']  tool: []  impl: []\n93\t=== modding-ugc [expert/runtime/Modding & UGC] parent=api-lifecycle-migration ws=gameplay profiles=['ugc'] targets=['client', 'headless-client', 'server', 'tools'] plats=None\n94\t  purpose: Mod and UGC support: mod SDK, content overrides via VFS layering, sandboxed mod scripting, UGC upload and moderation boundaries, mod compatibility across patches.\n95\t  nonresp: Sandbox policy -> security-engineering || Script VM -> scripting-runtime\n96\t  provides: []  consumes: ['C-VFS', 'C-SCRIPT', 'C-PLUGIN', 'C-SVC']  tool: []  impl: []\n97\t=== developer-experience-docs [cross-cutting/process/Developer Experience & Documentation] parent=engine-architect ws=governance profiles=['all'] targets=[] plats=None\n98\t  purpose: Documentation and developer experience: API reference, architecture docs, the sample-project ladder (2D → open-world online) that doubles as integration tests, templates, onboarding, doc testing, error-message standards, DX metrics.\n99\t  nonresp: ADR records -> architecture-governance || Iteration-time tooling -> hot-reload-iteration\n100\t  provides: []  consumes: []  tool: []  impl: []\n101\t=== ml-inference-runtime [expert/runtime/ML Inference Runtime] parent=gpu-platform-architect ws=rendering profiles=['lite3d', 'std3d'] targets=['client', 'headless-client', 'server', 'tools'] plats=None\n102\t  purpose: Runtime neural-network inference shared by neural rendering, animation, audio and AI: GPU (cooperative-vector / tensor) and CPU backends, model packaging and quantization, scheduling within frame budgets, determinism characteristics.\n103\t  nonresp: Vendor upscalers -> reconstruction-upscaling || In-shader (fused) networks -> shader-system || Neural feature design -> owning-skill || Model training -> external:ml-training\n104\t  provides: ['C-ML', 'C-MLGPU']  consumes: ['C-TASK', 'C-RHI?@C-MLGPU', 'C-RG?@C-MLGPU', 'C-PAL']  tool: []  impl: []\n105\t=== core-runtime-architect [lead/runtime/Core Runtime Architect] parent=engine-architect ws=foundation profiles=['all'] targets=['client', 'headless-client', 'server', 'tools'] plats=None\n106\t  purpose: Core runtime architecture: layering within core, module system and engine lifecycle (parallel boot, init graph, shutdown), configuration and cvars, error-handling and failure model, language and compiler feature policy.\n107\t  nonresp: Allocator design -> memory-allocators || Scheduler -> job-system-task-graph || Frame loop -> frame-orchestration\n108\t  provides: ['C-MOD', 'C-CFG', 'C-ERR', 'C-LIFETIME', 'C-IPC']  consumes: ['C-PAL', 'C-BASE', 'C-MEM', 'C-TYPES', 'C-SYNC', 'C-TASK', 'C-INSTR']  tool: []  impl: []\n109\t=== math-simd-numerics [expert/runtime/Math, SIMD & Numerics] parent=core-runtime-architect ws=foundation profiles=['all'] targets=['client', 'headless-client', 'server', 'tools'] plats=None\n110\t  purpose: Math and numerics: SIMD linear algebra, geometry and intersection primitives, computational geometry, numerical robustness, mixed and double precision, deterministic math, RNG and noise, curves, quantized formats, SPMD kernels with ISA dispatch.\n111\t  nonresp: Coordinate conventions decision -> engine-architect || Determinism rules -> determinism-replay\n112\t  provides: ['C-MATH']  consumes: ['C-PAL']  tool: []  impl: []\n113\t=== memory-allocators [expert/runtime/Memory & Allocators] parent=core-runtime-architect ws=foundation profiles=['all'] targets=['client', 'headless-client', 'server', 'tools'] plats=None\n114\t  purpose: Memory management: virtual memory, allocator families, thread-local and NUMA-aware allocation, tagging and attribution, budget enforcement mechanisms, fragmentation control, memory debugging, OOM policy, UMA accounting.\n115\t  nonresp: GPU heaps -> gpu-memory-resources || Budget numbers -> performance-architect\n116\t  provides: ['C-MEM']  consumes: ['C-PAL', 'C-BASE']  tool: []  impl: []\n117\t=== containers-core-types [expert/runtime/Containers & Core Types] parent=core-runtime-architect ws=foundation profiles=['all'] targets=['client', 'headless-client', 'server', 'tools'] plats=None\n118\t  purpose: Containers and core types: cache-friendly containers (open-addressing maps, inline and SoA containers, rings), strings and UTF-8, interned names, hashing, bit utilities, algorithms, explicit-ownership and view types.\n119\t  nonresp: Concurrent containers -> concurrency-primitives || Entity handles -> entity-object-model\n120\t  provides: ['C-TYPES']  consumes: ['C-MEM', 'C-BASE']  tool: []  impl: []\n121\t=== concurrency-primitives [expert/runtime/Concurrency Primitives] parent=core-runtime-architect ws=foundation profiles=['all'] targets=['client', 'headless-client', 'server', 'tools'] plats=None\n122\t  purpose: Memory model and atomics, synchronization primitives, lock-free and wait-free structures, safe memory reclamation, thread-safety annotations and model checking; reviewer for concurrent code engine-wide.\n123\t  nonresp: Scheduling -> job-system-task-graph || Concurrency test campaigns -> robustness-fuzzing\n124\t  provides: ['C-SYNC']  consumes: ['C-PAL', 'C-BASE']  tool: []  impl: []\n125\t=== job-system-task-graph [expert/runtime/Job System & Task Graph] parent=core-runtime-architect ws=foundation profiles=['all'] targets=['client', 'headless-client', 'server', 'tools'] plats=None\n126\t  purpose: Task-parallel execution: work-stealing scheduler, dependency task graphs, fibers and C++20 coroutines, priorities and QoS, heterogeneous-core and NUMA placement, IO/GPU completion integration, parallel algorithms, blocking policy.\n127\t  nonresp: Frame phase layout -> frame-orchestration || IO backends -> async-io-storage\n128\t  provides: ['C-TASK']  consumes: ['C-SYNC', 'C-PAL', 'C-BASE', 'C-MEM']  tool: []  impl: []\n129\t=== frame-orchestration [expert/runtime/Frame Orchestration & Time] parent=core-runtime-architect ws=foundation profiles=['all'] targets=['client', 'headless-client', 'server', 'tools'] plats=None\n130\t  purpose: The engine loop expressed as a task graph: frame pipelining across simulation, render and GPU, tick phases and sync points, fixed-step simulation with interpolation, time domains, latency and pacing control.\n131\t  nonresp: System ordering inside a phase -> ecs-runtime || Swapchain presentation -> rhi-core\n132\t  provides: ['C-FRAME', 'C-FLOW', 'C-PRESENT']  consumes: ['C-TASK', 'C-CFG', 'C-PAL']  tool: []  impl: []\n133\t=== entity-object-model [expert/runtime/Object Model & Identity] parent=core-runtime-architect ws=foundation profiles=['all'] targets=['client', 'headless-client', 'server', 'tools'] plats=None\n134\t  purpose: Object-model strategy and identity: generational entity IDs, stable GUIDs, hard/soft/weak references, the hybrid-model policy stating which data lives in ECS vs services vs asset objects vs UI, events and messaging.\n135\t  nonresp: ECS storage and queries -> ecs-runtime || Asset references -> content-pipeline-architect || Network IDs -> replication\n136\t  provides: ['C-ID']  consumes: ['C-TYPES', 'C-SYNC', 'C-LIFETIME']  tool: []  impl: []\n137\t=== ecs-runtime [expert/runtime/ECS Runtime] parent=core-runtime-architect ws=foundation profiles=['min2d', 'lite3d', 'std3d'] targets=['client', 'headless-client', 'server', 'tools'] plats=None\n138\t  purpose: ECS: storage (archetype chunks or sparse sets, chosen by ADR), queries, change detection, structural changes and command buffers, system scheduling with access-conflict analysis, relationships, singletons, authoring → runtime baking, debugging.\n139\t  nonresp: World partition -> world-architect || Transform propagation -> spatial-transforms || Object-model policy -> entity-object-model\n140\t  provides: ['C-ECS']  consumes: ['C-ID', 'C-TASK', 'C-FRAME', 'C-REFL?', 'C-SNAPSHOT', 'C-RELOAD?']  tool: []  impl: []\n141\t=== reflection-metadata [expert/runtime/Reflection & Metadata] parent=core-runtime-architect ws=foundation profiles=['all'] targets=['client', 'headless-client', 'server', 'tools'] plats=None\n142\t  purpose: Type registry, reflection generation (codegen now, C++26 static reflection when toolchains allow), attributes, the property system, script-binding substrate, dynamic invocation.\n143\t  nonresp: Serialization formats -> serialization-schema || Editor widgets -> editor-ui-framework || Script VM -> scripting-runtime\n144\t  provides: ['C-REFL']  consumes: ['C-TYPES']  tool: []  impl: []\n145\t=== serialization-schema [expert/runtime/Serialization & Schema Evolution] parent=core-runtime-architect ws=foundation profiles=['all'] targets=['client', 'headless-client', 'server', 'tools'] plats=None\n146\t  purpose: Binary and text formats, schema evolution and upgraders, in-place loadable layouts, canonical deterministic serialization, portability, and validation of untrusted input.\n147\t  nonresp: Package containers -> package-formats-vfs || Network bit packing -> replication || Save-game semantics -> persistence-save\n148\t  provides: ['C-SER']  consumes: ['C-REFL', 'C-TYPES']  tool: []  impl: []\n149\t=== platform-architect [lead/runtime/Platform Architect] parent=engine-architect ws=platform profiles=['all'] targets=['client', 'headless-client', 'server', 'tools'] plats=None\n150\t  purpose: Platform abstraction layer and porting strategy: OS services, CPU/GPU capability discovery, windowing, process lifecycle, capability tiers, and evaluation of new targets (web, cloud streaming).\n151\t  nonresp: Graphics API backends -> rhi-core || Store and online services -> platform-services || Toolchains -> build-system-toolchains\n152\t  provides: ['C-PAL', 'C-BASE']  consumes: []  tool: []  impl: []\n153\t=== platform-desktop [expert/runtime/Desktop & Handheld PC Platforms] parent=platform-architect ws=platform profiles=['all'] targets=['client', 'headless-client', 'server', 'tools'] plats=['pc']\n154\t  purpose: Windows, Linux, SteamOS and macOS integration: display modes, HDR and VRR capability, DPI, OS-specific IO and scheduling behavior, handheld-PC specifics, server host OS.\n155\t  nonresp: HDR signal encoding -> post-color-hdr || Swapchain -> rhi-core\n156\t  provides: []  consumes: ['C-PAL']  tool: []  impl: []\n157\t=== platform-console [expert/runtime/Console Platforms] parent=platform-architect ws=platform profiles=['all'] targets=['client', 'headless-client', 'server', 'tools'] plats=['pc']\n158\t  purpose: Console-class integration from platform-holder documentation: OS and memory model (UMA), suspend/resume, multi-user model, devkit workflows, platform requirements feeding certification.\n159\t  nonresp: Certification tracking -> certification-compliance || Console graphics API backend -> rhi-core\n160\t  provides: []  consumes: ['C-PAL', 'C-SVC', 'C-GPUTIER']  tool: []  impl: ['C-RHI']\n161\t=== platform-mobile [expert/runtime/Mobile Platforms] parent=platform-architect ws=platform profiles=['all'] targets=['client', 'headless-client', 'server', 'tools'] plats=['mobile', 'xr-standalone']\n162\t  purpose: iOS and Android (incl. Android-based standalone XR) integration: app lifecycle, thermal/power adaptivity, tile-based GPU implications, frame pacing, storage, notifications, deep links.\n163\t  nonresp: Render-graph TBDR optimizations -> render-graph-scheduling || Touch input -> input-devices-haptics\n164\t  provides: []  consumes: ['C-PAL']  tool: []  impl: []\n165\t=== platform-services [expert/runtime/Platform Services] parent=platform-architect ws=platform profiles=['all'] targets=['client', 'headless-client', 'server', 'tools'] plats=None\n166\t  purpose: First-party platform and store services: identity and sign-in, achievements and presence, entitlements and commerce through first-party stores, privileges and parental controls, social graph and invites, block/mute and text filtering, crossplay policy, leaderboards, cloud-save APIs, media capture, age and region policy enforcement.\n167\t  nonresp: Third-party/own backend & live-ops boundaries -> online-services-liveops || Game-server hosting -> dedicated-server || Save-game content -> persistence-save || Backend implementation -> external:backend\n168\t  provides: ['C-SVC']  consumes: ['C-PAL', 'C-TASK', 'C-CFG']  tool: []  impl: []\n169\t=== input-system [expert/runtime/Input Actions] parent=platform-architect ws=platform profiles=['all'] targets=['client', 'headless-client', 'server', 'tools'] plats=None\n170\t  purpose: Action-level input: mapping and context stacks, rebinding, buffering and latency accounting, local-multiplayer assignment, accessibility input options, UI navigation routing, per-device glyphs, recording and replay.\n171\t  nonresp: Device drivers and haptics -> input-devices-haptics || UI focus logic -> ui-architect\n172\t  provides: ['C-INPUT']  consumes: ['C-DEVICE?', 'C-FRAME', 'C-SER', 'C-A11Y']  tool: []  impl: []\n173\t=== input-devices-haptics [expert/runtime/Input Devices & Haptics] parent=platform-architect ws=platform profiles=['all'] targets=['client', 'tools'] plats=None\n174\t  purpose: Device layer: keyboard/mouse raw input, gamepads, touch and gestures, motion sensors, pen, hotplug and user pairing, haptics (rumble, HD haptics, adaptive triggers).\n175\t  nonresp: Action mapping -> input-system || XR controllers -> xr-runtime\n176\t  provides: ['C-DEVICE']  consumes: ['C-PAL']  tool: []  impl: []\n177\t=== xr-runtime [expert/runtime/XR Runtime] parent=platform-architect ws=platform profiles=['xr'] targets=['client', 'tools'] plats=None\n178\t  purpose: XR integration: OpenXR, stereo/multiview rendering hooks, foveation, reprojection and latency, XR input and hand tracking, comfort and safety requirements.\n179\t  nonresp: Render pipeline -> render-architect || Generic input actions -> input-system\n180\t  provides: ['C-XRVIEW']  consumes: ['C-PAL', 'C-INPUT', 'C-FRAME', 'C-PRESENT', 'C-VIEW', 'C-DEVICE', 'C-TEMPORAL?', 'C-A11Y']  tool: []  impl: []\n181\t=== content-pipeline-architect [lead/runtime/Content Pipeline Architect] parent=engine-architect ws=content profiles=['all'] targets=['client', 'headless-client', 'server', 'tools'] plats=None\n182\t  purpose: Asset identity and the content pipeline: asset registry and dependency graph, deterministic incremental per-platform cooking, the cook-step contract, derived-data cache and content-addressed store, distributed cooking, content validation.\n183\t  nonresp: Format-specific builders (shaders, animation, clusters…) -> shader-system || Runtime loading -> resource-streaming-architect || Import formats -> asset-import-interchange\n184\t  provides: ['C-ASSET', 'C-COOK']  consumes: ['C-SER', 'C-TASK', 'C-REFL']  tool: ['C-ML?']  impl: []\n185\t=== asset-import-interchange [expert/tool/Asset Import & Interchange] parent=content-pipeline-architect ws=content profiles=['all'] targets=['tools'] plats=None\n186\t  purpose: Importers and interchange: glTF, FBX, OpenUSD, texture and audio source formats, MaterialX/OpenPBR, DCC live link, reimport and source tracking, scan data.\n187\t  nonresp: Cooking -> content-pipeline-architect || Material model -> material-system\n188\t  provides: []  consumes: ['C-ASSET', 'C-COOK']  tool: []  impl: []\n189\t=== asset-cook-processors [expert/tool/Asset Cook Processors] parent=content-pipeline-architect ws=content profiles=['all'] targets=['tools'] plats=None\n190\t  purpose: Generic processors: texture processing and GPU texture-compression encoding, mesh optimization, hosting of collision and other domain builders under the cook contract.\n191\t  nonresp: Cluster DAG building -> virtualized-geometry-lod || Animation compression -> animation-runtime || Shader compilation -> shader-system\n192\t  provides: []  consumes: ['C-COOK', 'C-MATH', 'C-ML?']  tool: []  impl: []\n193\t=== resource-streaming-architect [lead/runtime/Resource & Streaming Architect] parent=engine-architect ws=content profiles=['all'] targets=['client', 'headless-client', 'server', 'tools'] plats=None\n194\t  purpose: Runtime resource model: handles and explicit lifetime, load requests with priority and deadline, dependency-aware loading, the streaming manager (budgets, eviction, prediction), fallbacks, no-stall loading.\n195\t  nonresp: IO backends -> async-io-storage || Package format -> package-formats-vfs || Texture-specific streaming -> texture-streaming-vt\n196\t  provides: ['C-RES']  consumes: ['C-ASSET', 'C-VFS', 'C-IO', 'C-TASK', 'C-GPUMEM?', 'C-FRAME', 'C-LIFETIME']  tool: []  impl: []\n197\t=== async-io-storage [expert/runtime/Async IO & Storage] parent=resource-streaming-architect ws=content profiles=['all'] targets=['client', 'headless-client', 'server', 'tools'] plats=None\n198\t  purpose: Async IO: io_uring, IOCP, DirectStorage and console backends, IO scheduling and queue depth, GPU decompression, memory-mapped IO, file-system abstraction, error handling.\n199\t  nonresp: Streaming decisions -> resource-streaming-architect || Codec choice -> package-formats-vfs\n200\t  provides: ['C-IO']  consumes: ['C-PAL', 'C-TASK', 'C-GPUMEM?']  tool: []  impl: []\n201\t=== package-formats-vfs [expert/runtime/Package Formats & VFS] parent=resource-streaming-architect ws=content profiles=['all'] targets=['client', 'headless-client', 'server', 'tools'] plats=None\n202\t  purpose: Package/container format and chunking, codec selection, VFS mount layering (base, patch, DLC, mods), encryption and signing, install-chunk layout.\n203\t  nonresp: Patch generation -> packaging-release-patching || Relocatable data layout -> serialization-schema\n204\t  provides: ['C-VFS']  consumes: ['C-IO', 'C-SER']  tool: []  impl: []\n205\t=== world-architect [lead/runtime/World Architect] parent=engine-architect ws=world profiles=['all'] targets=['client', 'headless-client', 'server', 'tools'] plats=None\n206\t  purpose: World representation strategy (data-oriented, no universal scene graph), partitioning and streaming cells, streaming sources, HLOD strategy, simulation LOD and significance, large-world coordinate policy, level transitions, server-side world streaming.\n207\t  nonresp: World document format -> world-data-model || Transform math -> spatial-transforms || HLOD mesh generation -> virtualized-geometry-lod\n208\t  provides: ['C-WORLD', 'C-SIGNIF', 'C-ENV']  consumes: ['C-SPATIAL', 'C-RES', 'C-ECS?', 'C-VIEW', 'C-FRAME']  tool: []  impl: []\n209\t=== world-data-model [expert/runtime/World Data Model] parent=world-architect ws=world profiles=['all'] targets=['client', 'headless-client', 'server', 'tools'] plats=None\n210\t  purpose: World and level documents, prefabs with nested overrides and variants, data layers, one-file-per-object layout for collaboration, level instances.\n211\t  nonresp: Serialization mechanics -> serialization-schema || Source-control workflows -> collaboration-version-control\n212\t  provides: []  consumes: ['C-WORLD', 'C-SER', 'C-ASSET', 'C-ID', 'C-RELOAD?']  tool: ['C-EDCMD', 'C-EDHOST']  impl: []\n213\t=== spatial-transforms [expert/runtime/Transforms & Spatial Queries] parent=world-architect ws=world profiles=['all'] targets=['client', 'headless-client', 'server', 'tools'] plats=None\n214\t  purpose: Transform representation and parallel hierarchy propagation, attachments, large-world coordinates implementation, generic spatial index and query service for non-physics consumers, spatial hashing.\n215\t  nonresp: Physics broadphase -> collision-detection || GPU culling -> geometry-pipeline\n216\t  provides: ['C-SPATIAL', 'C-VIEW']  consumes: ['C-MATH', 'C-ECS?', 'C-TASK', 'C-ID']  tool: []  impl: []\n217\t=== terrain [expert/runtime/Terrain] parent=world-architect ws=world profiles=['lite3d', 'std3d'] targets=['client', 'headless-client', 'server', 'tools'] plats=None\n218\t  purpose: Terrain end-to-end: representation, rendering, material layering, sculpt/paint tool logic, runtime deformation, collision data hand-off.\n219\t  nonresp: Virtual texturing core -> texture-streaming-vt || Viewport hosting -> world-editor-viewport || Collision algorithms -> collision-detection\n220\t  provides: []  consumes: ['C-WORLD?', 'C-RSCENE?', 'C-PHYS?', 'C-RES', 'C-MATIF?', 'C-ENV', 'C-INSTANCES?', 'C-VT?']  tool: ['C-EDCMD', 'C-EDHOST']  impl: ['C-ENV']\n221\t=== vegetation-foliage [expert/runtime/Vegetation & Foliage] parent=world-architect ws=world profiles=['lite3d', 'std3d'] targets=['client', 'headless-client', 'server', 'tools'] plats=None\n222\t  purpose: Vegetation instancing and rendering, procedural placement rules, wind and interaction, vegetation-specific LOD.\n223\t  nonresp: Generic PCG framework -> procedural-generation || Impostor generation -> virtualized-geometry-lod\n224\t  provides: []  consumes: ['C-WORLD?', 'C-RSCENE?', 'C-RES', 'C-ENV?', 'C-INSTANCES?', 'C-TEMPORAL?']  tool: ['C-EDCMD', 'C-EDHOST']  impl: []\n225\t=== water-ocean [expert/runtime/Water & Ocean] parent=world-architect ws=world profiles=['lite3d', 'std3d'] targets=['client', 'headless-client', 'server', 'tools'] plats=None\n226\t  purpose: Ocean spectral simulation, rivers, lakes and shorelines, water surface rendering, water queries for buoyancy.\n227\t  nonresp: Buoyancy dynamics -> character-physics || Fluid solvers -> fluid-simulation\n228\t  provides: []  consumes: ['C-WORLD?', 'C-RSCENE?', 'C-RG?', 'C-ENV', 'C-LIGHT?', 'C-GI?', 'C-TEMPORAL?']  tool: ['C-EDCMD', 'C-EDHOST']  impl: ['C-ENV']\n229\t=== atmosphere-weather [expert/runtime/Atmosphere, Volumetrics & Weather] parent=world-architect ws=world profiles=['lite3d', 'std3d'] targets=['client', 'headless-client', 'server', 'tools'] plats=None\n230\t  purpose: Sky and atmospheric scattering, volumetric clouds, volumetric fog and local media, weather state and surface response, time of day.\n231\t  nonresp: Sky lighting capture for GI -> global-illumination || Translucency compositing -> translucency-decals\n232\t  provides: ['C-ATMOS']  consumes: ['C-RSCENE?', 'C-RG?', 'C-FRAME', 'C-ENV', 'C-LIGHT?', 'C-TEMPORAL?']  tool: ['C-EDCMD', 'C-EDHOST']  impl: ['C-ENV']\n233\t=== procedural-generation [expert/runtime/Procedural Content Generation] parent=world-architect ws=world profiles=['openworld'] targets=['client', 'headless-client', 'server', 'tools'] plats=None\n234\t  purpose: Deterministic graph-based PCG framework usable in editor and at stream-in, placement and scattering rules, grammar and constraint methods; evaluates ML generation.\n235\t  nonresp: Foliage-specific rules -> vegetation-foliage || Graph editor UI -> graph-editor-framework\n236\t  provides: []  consumes: ['C-WORLD', 'C-DET', 'C-ML?', 'C-INSTANCES?']  tool: ['C-COOK', 'C-EDCMD', 'C-EDHOST', 'C-GRAPH']  impl: []\n237\t=== render-architect [lead/runtime/Render Architect] parent=engine-architect ws=rendering profiles=['all'] targets=['client', 'tools'] plats=None\n238\t  purpose: Rendering architecture: pipeline organization, shading-path choice (forward+, deferred, visibility buffer), render-feature contract, render scene and world→render sync, scalability tiers from 2D mobile to path-traced, multi-view, debug modes, render threading.\n239\t  nonresp: API backends -> gpu-platform-architect || Pass scheduling -> render-graph-scheduling || Individual features (GI, shadows…) -> owning-skill\n240\t  provides: ['C-RSCENE']  consumes: ['C-RG', 'C-SPATIAL', 'C-MATIF', 'C-FRAME', 'C-FLOW', 'C-VIEW', 'C-GPUTIER', 'C-ECS?', 'C-XRVIEW?', 'C-INSTANCES?', 'C-A11Y']  tool: []  impl: []\n241\t=== rhi-core [expert/runtime/RHI Core] parent=gpu-platform-architect ws=rendering profiles=['all'] targets=['client', 'tools'] plats=None\n242\t  purpose: Render hardware interface over D3D12, Vulkan, Metal, console APIs and WebGPU: queues and command recording, synchronization, bindless descriptors, PSOs and PSO caching, presentation, capability tiers, GPU crash breadcrumbs, driver workarounds.\n243\t  nonresp: GPU memory allocation -> gpu-memory-resources || Barrier planning -> render-graph-scheduling || Shader compilation -> shader-system || Per-API backend code -> ['rhi-d3d12', 'rhi-vulkan', 'rhi-metal', 'rhi-webgpu', 'platform-console']\n244\t  provides: ['C-RHI']  consumes: ['C-PAL', 'C-SYNC', 'C-PRESENT', 'C-FRAME']  tool: []  impl: []\n245\t=== gpu-memory-resources [expert/runtime/GPU Memory & Resources] parent=gpu-platform-architect ws=rendering profiles=['all'] targets=['client', 'tools'] plats=None\n246\t  purpose: GPU heaps and suballocation, residency and overcommit, upload/readback rings, sparse/reserved resources, GPU memory budgeting and defragmentation, lifetimes decoupled from frame boundaries.\n247\t  nonresp: Transient aliasing plans -> render-graph-scheduling || Texture streaming policy -> texture-streaming-vt\n248\t  provides: ['C-GPUMEM']  consumes: ['C-RHI', 'C-GPUTIER', 'C-LIFETIME']  tool: []  impl: []\n249\t=== render-graph-scheduling [expert/runtime/Render Graph & GPU Scheduling] parent=gpu-platform-architect ws=rendering profiles=['all'] targets=['client', 'tools'] plats=None\n250\t  purpose: Render graph declaration and compilation, automatic barriers, transient aliasing, async compute and multi-queue scheduling, TBDR pass merging, history resources, work-graph integration, general GPU compute, readback contract.\n251\t  nonresp: Heap allocation -> gpu-memory-resources || Feature passes -> render-architect\n252\t  provides: ['C-RG']  consumes: ['C-RHI', 'C-GPUMEM', 'C-TASK']  tool: []  impl: []\n253\t=== shader-system [expert/runtime/Shader System] parent=gpu-platform-architect ws=rendering profiles=['all'] targets=['client', 'tools'] plats=None\n254\t  purpose: Shading language and dialect, compilation toolchain, permutations, reflection and binding layouts, interop headers, caches and distributed compilation, hot reload, shader debugging, PSO-list gathering.\n255\t  nonresp: Material graphs -> material-system || Runtime PSO cache -> rhi-core\n256\t  provides: ['C-SHADER']  consumes: ['C-RHI', 'C-GPUTIER', 'C-ML?', 'C-RELOAD?']  tool: ['C-COOK']  impl: []\n257\t=== material-system [expert/runtime/Material System] parent=render-architect ws=rendering profiles=['all'] targets=['client', 'tools'] plats=None\n258\t  purpose: Material model (OpenPBR-class, layered), material graph → shader code generation, instances and parameters, quality tiers, material validation; evaluates neural materials.\n259\t  nonresp: BRDF research reference -> research-evidence || Graph editor UI -> graph-editor-framework || Shader compiler -> shader-system\n260\t  provides: ['C-MATIF']  consumes: ['C-SHADER', 'C-ASSET', 'C-MLGPU?', 'C-GPUTIER']  tool: ['C-EDCMD', 'C-EDHOST', 'C-GRAPH']  impl: []\n261\t=== geometry-pipeline [expert/runtime/Geometry Submission Pipeline] parent=render-architect ws=rendering profiles=['lite3d', 'std3d'] targets=['client', 'tools'] plats=None\n262\t  purpose: Instance scene and geometry submission for every 3D tier: persistent instance data with batched delta updates, the CPU-culled batched/instanced path (first-class on TBDR/mobile and lite3d), and the GPU-driven path (GPU culling, indirect/mesh shaders, visibility buffer) for desktop/console tiers.\n263\t  nonresp: Cluster LOD -> virtualized-geometry-lod || Render-scene contract -> render-architect\n264\t  provides: ['C-INSTANCES']  consumes: ['C-RSCENE', 'C-RG', 'C-SHADER', 'C-GPUMEM', 'C-GPUTIER', 'C-GEOLOD?', 'C-TEMPORAL?']  tool: []  impl: []\n265\t=== virtualized-geometry-lod [expert/runtime/Virtualized Geometry & LOD] parent=render-architect ws=rendering profiles=['lite3d', 'std3d'] targets=['client', 'tools'] plats=None\n266\t  purpose: All geometric LOD: cluster hierarchies and virtualized geometry, cluster DAG building, software micro-polygon rasterization, cluster streaming, discrete LOD, HLOD proxies and impostors, deforming-geometry LOD, displacement.\n267\t  nonresp: HLOD strategy -> world-architect || Generic mesh optimization -> asset-cook-processors || RT acceleration structures -> ray-tracing-infrastructure\n268\t  provides: ['C-GEOLOD']  consumes: ['C-RSCENE', 'C-RG', 'C-RES', 'C-RT?', 'C-INSTANCES']  tool: ['C-COOK', 'C-EDCMD', 'C-EDHOST']  impl: []\n269\t=== texture-streaming-vt [expert/runtime/Textures & Virtual Texturing] parent=render-architect ws=rendering profiles=['all'] targets=['client', 'tools'] plats=None\n270\t  purpose: Runtime texture formats, mip streaming, sampler-feedback streaming, virtual texturing, streaming-friendly cooked layout; evaluates neural texture compression.\n271\t  nonresp: Texture encoding in cook -> asset-cook-processors || Streaming manager -> resource-streaming-architect\n272\t  provides: ['C-VT']  consumes: ['C-RES', 'C-GPUMEM', 'C-RG', 'C-ML?', 'C-MLGPU?']  tool: ['C-COOK']  impl: []\n273\t=== direct-lighting-shadows [expert/runtime/Direct Lighting & Shadows] parent=render-architect ws=rendering profiles=['lite3d', 'std3d'] targets=['client', 'tools'] plats=None\n274\t  purpose: Light types and physical units, clustered light culling, stochastic many-light sampling, area lights, cascaded, virtual and ray-traced shadows, contact shadows, light profiles.\n275\t  nonresp: Indirect lighting -> global-illumination || Denoisers -> reconstruction-upscaling\n276\t  provides: ['C-LIGHT']  consumes: ['C-RSCENE', 'C-RG', 'C-RT?', 'C-TEMPORAL', 'C-INSTANCES?', 'C-GEOLOD?']  tool: []  impl: []\n277\t=== global-illumination [expert/runtime/Global Illumination & Reflections] parent=render-architect ws=rendering profiles=['lite3d', 'std3d'] targets=['client', 'tools'] plats=None\n278\t  purpose: Indirect lighting across tiers: baked lightmaps, probe volumes, screen-space GI and AO, surface/radiance-cache hybrid GI, ReSTIR GI, reflections, sky lighting, specular occlusion, SDF scene representations.\n