stration of the code → content → package pipeline.\n483\t  nonresp: Build system implementation -> build-system-toolchains || CI pipelines -> ci-cd-automation || Packaging -> packaging-release-patching\n484\t  provides: ['C-RELEASE']  consumes: ['C-BUILD', 'C-PKG']  tool: ['C-COOK']  impl: []\n485\t=== build-system-toolchains [expert/tool/Build System & Toolchains] parent=build-release-architect ws=release profiles=['all'] targets=['tools'] plats=None\n486\t  purpose: Build graph, compiler and toolchain matrix, C++ modules/unity/PCH, compile caching and distribution, codegen integration, third-party dependencies, static analysis, build configurations.\n487\t  nonresp: CI orchestration -> ci-cd-automation || Supply-chain policy -> security-engineering\n488\t  provides: ['C-BUILD']  consumes: []  tool: []  impl: []\n489\t=== ci-cd-automation [expert/tool/CI/CD & Automation] parent=build-release-architect ws=release profiles=['all'] targets=['tools'] plats=None\n490\t  purpose: CI pipelines, build farm and artifact storage, pre-submit and merge gating, symbol servers, device-farm orchestration, developer CLI and automation.\n491\t  nonresp: What tests exist -> test-architect || Perf thresholds -> performance-architect\n492\t  provides: []  consumes: ['C-BUILD', 'C-COOK']  tool: []  impl: []\n493\t=== packaging-release-patching [expert/tool/Packaging, Patching & Release] parent=build-release-architect ws=release profiles=['all'] targets=['tools'] plats=None\n494\t  purpose: Platform packaging and signing, store-submission artifacts, delta/chunk patching, DLC, install-on-demand, client/server/content version compatibility, CDN boundary, release rollback.\n495\t  nonresp: Package runtime format -> package-formats-vfs || Certification tracking -> certification-compliance\n496\t  provides: ['C-PKG']  consumes: ['C-VFS', 'C-BUILD', 'C-SVC', 'C-COOK', 'C-RELEASE']  tool: []  impl: []\n497\t=== runtime-scalability [expert/runtime/Runtime Scalability & Governor] parent=core-runtime-architect ws=foundation profiles=['all'] targets=['client', 'headless-client', 'server', 'tools'] plats=None\n498\t  purpose: Runtime scalability machinery: device-profile application, the registry of scalability knobs and actuators, first-run hardware auto-detect, and the closed-loop runtime governor that consumes frame-time, thermal/power and memory-pressure signals and drives registered actuators (dynamic resolution, significance, VFX, animation rate, worker count) with priorities and hysteresis.\n499\t  nonresp: Budget numbers and tier definitions -> performance-architect || Hardware→tier device database -> platform-architect || Each actuator's own implementation -> owning-skill\n500\t  provides: ['C-SCALE']  consumes: ['C-CFG', 'C-PAL', 'C-INSTR', 'C-TASK']  tool: []  impl: []\n501\t=== voxel-worlds [expert/runtime/Voxel & Buildable Worlds] parent=world-architect ws=world profiles=['sandbox'] targets=['client', 'headless-client', 'server', 'tools'] plats=None\n502\t  purpose: Chunked voxel/block worlds end to end: sparse storage and compression, meshing and remeshing on edit, runtime edit replication and persistence hand-off, block light propagation.\n503\t  nonresp: Player construction gameplay (snapping, structural integrity) -> gameplay-systems-toolkit || Heightfield terrain -> terrain || Replication mechanics -> replication\n504\t  provides: []  consumes: ['C-WORLD', 'C-ENV', 'C-SPATIAL', 'C-RES', 'C-RSCENE?', 'C-PHYS?', 'C-REP?', 'C-SAVE?']  tool: []  impl: ['C-ENV']\n505\t=== gpu-platform-architect [lead/runtime/GPU Platform Architect] parent=engine-architect ws=rendering profiles=['all'] targets=['client', 'tools'] plats=None\n506\t  purpose: GPU platform architecture shared by every renderer tier: layering of RHI, GPU memory, render graph, shader system, ray-query and inference infrastructure; the GPU feature-tier model (binding, pipeline-state, queue, mesh, RT, tensor tiers) and API baselines per hardware tier; task-based parallel command recording.\n507\t  nonresp: Rendering pipeline and features -> render-architect || Individual API backends -> ['rhi-d3d12', 'rhi-vulkan', 'rhi-metal', 'rhi-webgpu'] || Frames in flight / thread existence -> frame-orchestration\n508\t  provides: ['C-GPUTIER']  consumes: ['C-RHI', 'C-PAL']  tool: []  impl: []\n509\t=== rhi-d3d12 [expert/runtime/RHI D3D12 backend] parent=gpu-platform-architect ws=rendering profiles=['all'] targets=['client', 'tools'] plats=['pc']\n510\t  purpose: Implements C-RHI on D3D12 (Agility SDK features: enhanced barriers, work graphs, SM 6.x, GPU upload heaps); owns its validation-layer runs and vendor/driver quirks.\n511\t  nonresp: RHI abstraction & capability model -> rhi-core || Other API backends -> rhi-core\n512\t  provides: []  consumes: ['C-PAL', 'C-SYNC', 'C-GPUTIER']  tool: []  impl: ['C-RHI']\n513\t=== rhi-vulkan [expert/runtime/RHI Vulkan backend] parent=gpu-platform-architect ws=rendering profiles=['all'] targets=['client', 'tools'] plats=['pc', 'mobile', 'xr-standalone']\n514\t  purpose: Implements C-RHI on Vulkan (profiles incl. Android Baseline, descriptor buffers/heaps, synchronization2, dynamic rendering); owns its validation-layer runs and vendor/driver quirks.\n515\t  nonresp: RHI abstraction & capability model -> rhi-core || Other API backends -> rhi-core\n516\t  provides: []  consumes: ['C-PAL', 'C-SYNC', 'C-GPUTIER']  tool: []  impl: ['C-RHI']\n517\t=== rhi-metal [expert/runtime/RHI Metal backend] parent=gpu-platform-architect ws=rendering profiles=['all'] targets=['client', 'tools'] plats=['pc', 'mobile']\n518\t  purpose: Implements C-RHI on Metal 3/4 (argument buffers, residency sets, MTL4 command model); owns its validation-layer runs and vendor/driver quirks.\n519\t  nonresp: RHI abstraction & capability model -> rhi-core || Other API backends -> rhi-core\n520\t  provides: []  consumes: ['C-PAL', 'C-SYNC', 'C-GPUTIER']  tool: []  impl: ['C-RHI']\n521\t=== rhi-webgpu [expert/runtime/RHI WebGPU backend] parent=gpu-platform-architect ws=rendering profiles=['all'] targets=['client', 'tools'] plats=['web']\n522\t  purpose: Implements C-RHI on WebGPU (bind groups, implicit sync, limits tiers); owns its validation-layer runs and vendor/driver quirks.\n523\t  nonresp: RHI abstraction & capability model -> rhi-core || Other API backends -> rhi-core\n524\t  provides: []  consumes: ['C-PAL', 'C-SYNC', 'C-GPUTIER']  tool: []  impl: ['C-RHI']\n525\t=== media-playback [expert/runtime/Media & Video Playback] parent=render-architect ws=rendering profiles=['all'] targets=['client', 'tools'] plats=None\n526\t  purpose: Pre-rendered video playback end to end: hardware/software decode backends, A/V sync against the audio clock, video surfaces for UI, world and cinematics, HDR video, package streaming.\n527\t  nonresp: Movie rendering (producing video) -> cinematics-sequencer || Audio mixing -> audio-dsp-mixing\n528\t  provides: ['C-VIDEO']  consumes: ['C-IO', 'C-RES', 'C-GPUMEM', 'C-AUDIO', 'C-FRAME', 'C-RG']  tool: []  impl: []\n529\t=== vehicle-physics [expert/runtime/Vehicle Physics] parent=physics-architect ws=simulation profiles=['vehicles'] targets=['client', 'headless-client', 'server', 'tools'] plats=None\n530\t  purpose: Vehicle dynamics: wheeled vehicles (tires, suspension, drivetrain), aerodynamic surfaces and flight models, orbital mechanics, watercraft hydrodynamics, vehicle-specific prediction and force-feedback sources.\n531\t  nonresp: Character controllers -> character-physics || Generic buoyancy -> rigid-body-dynamics || Netcode model -> prediction-rollback\n532\t  provides: []  consumes: ['C-PHYS', 'C-DET', 'C-ENV?', 'C-DEVICE?', 'C-PREDICT?']  tool: []  impl: []\n533\t=== physics-tools [expert/tool/Physics Tools] parent=physics-architect ws=simulation profiles=['min2d', 'lite3d', 'std3d'] targets=['tools'] plats=None\n534\t  purpose: Physics authoring and debugging tools: collision authoring, physics-asset/ragdoll and constraint editors, the physics visual debugger/recorder, simulate-in-editor, vehicle and controller tuning, 2D collision-shape editing.\n535\t  nonresp: Collision algorithms -> collision-detection || Editor host & transactions -> editor-architect\n536\t  provides: []  consumes: ['C-EDCMD', 'C-EDHOST', 'C-PHYS', 'C-INSTR', 'C-REPLAY?']  tool: []  impl: []\n537\t=== character-movement [expert/runtime/Character Movement] parent=gameplay-architect ws=gameplay profiles=['min2d', 'lite3d', 'std3d'] targets=['client', 'headless-client', 'server', 'tools'] plats=None\n538\t  purpose: Character movement as one system at the junction of input, physics, animation and netcode: movement modes, step/slope rules, root-motion consumption and authority, networked predicted/reconciled movement with a resimulatable move API, mount/vehicle transitions, 2D platformer movement.\n539\t  nonresp: Collide-and-slide controller primitive -> character-physics || Generic prediction machinery -> prediction-rollback || Animation selection -> motion-synthesis\n540\t  provides: ['C-MOVE']  consumes: ['C-GAME', 'C-PHYS', 'C-INPUT', 'C-ANIM?', 'C-PREDICT?', 'C-DET']  tool: []  impl: []\n541\t=== gameplay-data [expert/runtime/Gameplay Data & Tuning] parent=gameplay-architect ws=gameplay profiles=['all'] targets=['client', 'headless-client', 'server', 'tools'] plats=None\n542\t  purpose: Designer-owned data: typed data tables and row references, curve assets, tuning assets with inheritance and per-platform/difficulty variants, spreadsheet round-trip, balance simulation, and live data hotfixes through remote overrides.\n543\t  nonresp: Serialization mechanics -> serialization-schema || Remote-config service -> online-services-liveops || Tabular editing widgets -> editor-ui-framework\n544\t  provides: ['C-GAMEDATA']  consumes: ['C-REFL', 'C-ASSET', 'C-SER', 'C-LIVE?', 'C-CFG']  tool: ['C-EDCMD', 'C-EDHOST']  impl: []\n545\t=== narrative-dialogue [expert/runtime/Narrative & Dialogue] parent=gameplay-architect ws=gameplay profiles=['all'] targets=['client', 'headless-client', 'server', 'tools'] plats=None\n546\t  purpose: The dialogue line model and narrative runtime shared by VO, subtitles, lip sync, localization, cinematics and AI: line database with stable IDs, branching dialogue runtime and narrative-middleware interchange, narrative fact store with save/replication participation, barks and response rules, recording scripts and placeholder VO.\n547\t  nonresp: Quest content -> external:game-team || VO playback -> audio-content-runtime || String formatting -> localization-i18n\n548\t  provides: ['C-DIALOGUE']  consumes: ['C-LOC', 'C-SER', 'C-ID', 'C-SAVE?', 'C-REP?', 'C-A11Y']  tool: ['C-EDCMD', 'C-EDHOST', 'C-GRAPH']  impl: []\n549\t=== reference-games [expert/process/Reference Games] parent=program-orchestration ws=governance profiles=['all'] targets=[] plats=None\n550\t  purpose: The reference-game ladder (one representative game per configuration) used as milestone and release gate, representative production-scale content sets, and the internal playtest and dogfood loop.\n551\t  nonresp: Teaching samples -> developer-experience-docs || Benchmark harness -> perf-benchmarking\n552\t  provides: []  consumes: []  tool: []  impl: []\n553\t=== platform-web [expert/runtime/Web Platform] parent=platform-architect ws=platform profiles=['minimal', 'min2d', 'lite3d'] targets=['client', 'tools'] plats=['web']\n554\t  purpose: Web target (WASM + WebGPU): threads and cross-origin isolation, memory limits, OPFS/IndexedDB storage, HTTP streaming delivery, user-gesture rules for audio/pointer/fullscreen, browser transport constraints.\n555\t  nonresp: WebGPU backend -> rhi-webgpu || Browser transports -> network-transport\n556\t  provides: []  consumes: ['C-PAL']  tool: []  impl: []\n557\t=== online-services-liveops [expert/runtime/Online Services & Live Ops] parent=platform-architect ws=platform profiles=['all'] targets=['client', 'headless-client', 'server', 'tools'] plats=None\n558\t  purpose: Integration boundary to third-party and own online backends and live operations: matchmaking/lobby/session boundary, remote config and feature flags, live events and experiments, service-hosted voice/text chat sessions, moderation (UGC, chat, generated content), wallet and ads boundaries, trusted time, remote generative-AI/inference boundary, service emulators and outage injection for tests.\n559\t  nonresp: First-party platform services -> platform-services || Backend implementation -> external:backend || Game-server hosting -> dedicated-server\n560\t  provides: ['C-LIVE']  consumes: ['C-PAL', 'C-TASK', 'C-CFG', 'C-SVC?']  tool: []  impl: []\n561\t=== memory-performance [expert/process/Memory Performance] parent=performance-architect ws=performance profiles=['all'] targets=[] plats=None\n562\t  purpose: Memory as its own performance discipline: whole-process CPU+GPU+UMA footprint analysis per tier, snapshot capture and diffing, content-level attribution per asset/cell/feature, transition peak analysis, fragmentation over time; reviewer for the memory-usage obligation.\n563\t  nonresp: Allocator mechanisms -> memory-allocators || Budget numbers -> performance-architect\n564\t  provides: []  consumes: []  tool: []  impl: []\n565\t=== simulation-validation [expert/process/Simulation & Systems Validation] parent=test-architect ws=quality profiles=['all'] targets=[] plats=None\n566\t  purpose: Runs the objective validation that domain owners define for simulation-class systems: physics stability and reference suites, simulation golden traces, animation error suites, audio offline-render suites, and deterministic network simulation for prediction/replication correctness, mirroring what render-validation does for rendering.\n567\t  nonresp: Defining each domain's oracles -> owning-skill || Determinism matrix definition -> determinism-replay\n568\t  provides: []  consumes: []  tool: []  impl: []\n569\t=== engine-product-management [orchestrator/process/Engine Product Management] parent=engine-architect ws=governance profiles=['all'] targets=[] plats=None\n570\t  purpose: The engine as a product for game teams: roadmap and prioritization across game-team requirements, bug and feature intake with triage SLAs, release notes and upgrade guides, the customer-project corpus that validates each engine release, and the engine licensing model.\n571\t  nonresp: Architecture decisions -> engine-architect || Work scheduling -> program-orchestration || Engine release mechanics -> build-release-architect\n572\t  provides: ['C-PROD']  consumes: []  tool: []  impl: []\n573\t"}]},"uuid":"da8d4374-222f-4af8-93d2-b0c2161ebb48","timestamp":"2026-09-29T16:20:55.844Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ee482245-ad1e-4715-9b31-f8dde26bded7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"remote_mobile","cwd":"/home/user/skills","sessionId":"64f15158-6a4e-5bdf-8a90-7f2bd7b05b82","version":"2.1.284","gitBranch":"claude/engine-skill-framework-phase1"}
